### Build Peculiarities

- **Two-phase compilation**: `maven-compiler-plugin` runs a `recompile` execution at `process-classes` phase because `camel-component-maven-plugin` generates sources at the same phase — code must be recompiled to pick up generated Camel component metadata
- **Annotation processors** (order matters): Lombok → Lombok-MapStruct binding → MapStruct processor
- **Spring Boot repackage**: uses classifier `exec` (produces `qip-engine-*-exec.jar`)
- **Docker**: base image `alpine/java:21-jdk`, port 8080, non-root user (UID 10001), JVM: `-Xmx832m`

### Platform Context

This service is part of the **Qubership Integration Platform (QIP)** — a microservices-based integration platform. See `README.md` for the repository layout.

#### Direct Dependencies (this service consumes)

| Service | Protocol | What For |
|---|---|---|
| **Runtime Catalog** | REST (`POST /v1/catalog/domains/{domain}/deployments/update`) | Fetch chain deployment descriptors and configuration updates |
| **Runtime Catalog** | REST (`GET /v1/models/{id}/dto/jar`) | Download compiled external library JARs |
| **Consul** | REST (`/v1/kv/*`, `/v1/session/*`, `/v1/txn`) | Configuration (prefix `config/{NAMESPACE}/`), deployment state coordination, distributed sessions |
| **OpenSearch** | HTTP | Record session execution data (element-level traces) in index `qip-elements-{namespace}` |
| **PostgreSQL** | JDBC | 3 databases: `engine_checkpoints_db` (sessions/checkpoints), `engine_qrtz_db` (Quartz scheduler), `engine` (main) |
| **Control Plane** | REST | Register public/private engine routes, egress gateway routes |
| **Kafka** (optional) | Camel component | Integration chains + optional session data streaming |
| **RabbitMQ** (optional) | Camel AMQP | Integration chains |
| **Redis** (optional) | Redis protocol | Idempotency cache |

#### Services That Depend on This

| Service | How |
|---|---|
| **Runtime Catalog** | Calls `GET /v1/engine/live-exchanges` and `DELETE /v1/engine/live-exchanges/{deploymentId}/{exchangeId}` to monitor/kill running exchanges |
| **UI** | Calls Engine APIs via Nginx proxy (`/api/*/engine/*`) |

#### Sibling Service: Micro Engine

**qubership-integration-micro-engine** is a Quarkus-based alternative to this Spring Boot engine. Same functionality, different framework. They share the same API contracts (`/v1/engine/*`), same database schemas, same Consul/OpenSearch integration patterns. Key difference: Quarkus provides faster startup and lower memory for cloud-native deployments.
